      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "# Milestone 2 delivery: Concordia (CAP) - First Executable Slices in Both Proving Domains\n\nHello everyone — the Milestone 2 deliverables are complete and public in the project repository: **https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia** (Apache-2.0, branch `dev`).\n\nM2 contains two reference formats, one per proving domain: a majority vote with vote privacy, and a sealed-bid first-price auction where the payment is settled with canton coin, and a simulated registry built on `TestTokenV2` issues the lot.\n\n**What changed since M1.** The auction interfaces were built. Both reference flows were built, each carrying its privacy claim. [State pinning in cap-governance was improved](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/cap-governance/DESIGN.md#how-it-generalizes-from-splice), and the [Baby-dso reference flow](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/examples/governance/baby-dso/DEMOS.md#demo-use-case) changed to show that improvement.\n\n## Milestone verification\n\nDaml SDK 3.4.11 via `dpm`, from the repository root. Run instructions, in-memory and on a sandbox, are in [`README.md#running-the-demos`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/README.md#running-the-demos). The privacy claims can be checked by reading the `whoSeesWhat` assertions (these assertions do not catch divulgence, that can be checked by opening the same scripts in Daml Studio).\n\n\n| Slice | Check | Expected output | Guarantees |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| all packages | `dpm build --all` | every package in `multi-package.yaml` compiles | — |\n| [majority-vote reference](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/tree/dev/examples/governance/private-majority-vote/impl) | `dpm test --package-root examples/governance/private-majority-vote/demo` | every script reports **`ok`** | [what each script claims](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/examples/governance/private-majority-vote/DEMOS.md#security-claims) |\n| [sealed-bid auction reference](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/tree/dev/examples/auctions/sealed-bid-first-price/impl) | `dpm test --package-root examples/auctions/sealed-bid-first-price/demo` | every script reports **`ok`** | [what each script claims](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/examples/auctions/sealed-bid-first-price/DEMOS.md#security-claims) |\n| [Baby-dso reference](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/tree/dev/examples/governance/baby-dso/cap) | `dpm test --package-root examples/governance/baby-dso/cap/demo` | every script reports **`ok`** | [what each script claims](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/examples/governance/baby-dso/DEMOS.md#security-claims) |\n| all slices, on a ledger | [`./scripts/sandbox-test.sh`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/scripts/sandbox-test.sh) | every script reports **`SUCCESS`** | the same claims |\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\nWe're happy to answer questions here or walk through any part of either slice.\nWe would greatly value your feedback.\n\n",
